{"title":"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 31","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02a864f3a703df90f49bdc19bf10b3eac8636ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC:CB$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeed4747bc966b093ca8740cc9bd952cf39c891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. The bisector of the exterior angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> extended at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> \n(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />). The ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b73dfdde1bc633e93c5562cb4730dcbc1fa1be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA:AB$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d0651cd7d19786334845cc311e859049943147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1:3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3:4 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4:3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 3:1 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 7:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"469\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52cce542e1e5db3286077999ca9d2232da209c64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(40,0)--(16,18)--(0,0)); draw((40,0)--(64,72)--(16,18)); draw((40,0)--(160,0)--(64,72),dotted); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;B&quot;,(0,0),SW); dot((16,18)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(16,18),NW); dot((40,0)); label(&quot;C&quot;,(40,0),S); dot((64,72)); label(&quot;P&quot;,(64,72),N); dot((160,0)); label(&quot;X&quot;,(160,0),SE);  label(&quot;$4n$&quot;,(20,0),S); label(&quot;$3n$&quot;,(33,17)); label(&quot;$4an-4n$&quot;,(100,0),S); label(&quot;$3an$&quot;,(112,36),NE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"142\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed772e60a5acdad0777a20f80ba45721df354634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 3n$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe3cf9235cc0e39fc785a205711c9f78b3ef44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />.  Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca40638cf9d1cd112b248043d670d19f8035774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\parallel PX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />.  By AA Similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f520e7944a795965209e911e146eaa214abe260.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle PBX$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/48707dcfd0e9d21cd33a92eb56992ae46055f36f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX = 3an$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/8427db53a39fdc3bcb201a5ac086db34c01c02d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = 4an$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e93bae5f3ccc9a50245dbfaca7f15bc54df9cb6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX = 4an - 4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAlso, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d276b6e61e106081b773f4663051b99f527c714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = a$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1965596fe9913d4b2617c0e10d0fc9a0c9ce38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = b$\" width=\"87\" height=\"13\" />.  Since the angles of a triangle add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f964048c3c16ce6fb415a04d99cc023656cf3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA = 180-a-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"169\" height=\"13\" />.  By Exterior Angle Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1ba6074f0bbe750c6a0aafcacfc50a7153235e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACX = a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d13fd509f3062449aaea6e10e1040b1d585063f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa42dc70d2a6cc8b53622c2195da64b7f65f4e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a93666befaf4e183f6f8e72654583e46e9a45268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PCX = \\frac{a+b}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"39\" />.  Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca40638cf9d1cd112b248043d670d19f8035774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\parallel PX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc655f8da4cb3379696e774c4b4a24c9b08a6ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BXP = 180 - a - b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"172\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/6293f91393b38c9245c11b917705afb5008e5aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPX = \\frac{a+b}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb935aadc14e5d47641ead152f0527747de70334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CPX$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">isosceles triangle</a>.\n</p><p><br />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb935aadc14e5d47641ead152f0527747de70334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CPX$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/89467ca93f879c2a3eadd012f4b820238a900983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX = CX$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83fdd8d854165b40da673cee8c7517ce23faa4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4an - 4n = 3an$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" />.  That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f98b3f405113241659d8c8db2ea3480346db4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed39aa2f189a9504f7415257eed6bb5900b73cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB = 4 \\cdot AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4d8ddbdb5679a429351ba27e0d941176da15ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA = PB - AB = 3 \\cdot AB$\" width=\"205\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5f1e1472494446450961ba25104fa71a09d222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA : AB = 3:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />, and it can be verified (or obtained) by making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> a 3-4-5 right triangle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME\" title=\"1961 AHSME\">1961 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1961 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1961\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">Problem 32</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\"